cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  MAGPIE: Multi-Primitive Bimanual Garment Folding from Crumpled States
  with Pixel-based Flow Matching Policies
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: https://github.com/halid1020/learning_garment_manipulation
abstract: >-
  A data-driven system for bimanual garment manipulation covering flattening,
  canonicalisation-alignment and folding from crumpled states. MAGPIE is a
  multi-primitive imitation-learning policy in which an MLP classifier selects one
  of four action primitives and per-primitive Optimal-Transport Conditional Flow
  Matching networks generate the continuous parameters. LaGarNet is a
  goal-conditioned latent-dynamics model used for model-predictive control.
keywords:
  - robotic manipulation
  - deformable object manipulation
  - garment folding
  - imitation learning
  - flow matching
  - bimanual manipulation
